From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDNA4-MacOS contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] radv/darwin: expose only native queues and avoid null
 member arithmetic

RDNA4N Submit's cs_parse accepts only GFX instance 0, ring 0. The canned
Linux compute ring masks otherwise make RADV advertise asynchronous
compute queues whose submissions the kernel rejects. Hide those queues
on native/mock connections; compute dispatch remains available on the
general GFX queue. Keep HOST_BO's synthetic device information intact.

Use offsetof in the vendored list helper. Its null-pointer member
expression trips UBSan when the VA manager is destroyed, even without
allocating a BO.

Neither fix changes the gfx1200 topology or memory sizing. Native memory
queries already use QueryInfo's pool totals and per-session budget.
---
 src/amd/common/darwin/ac_darwin_drm.c           | 6 +++++-
 src/amd/common/darwin/libdrm_util_double_list.h | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/common/darwin/ac_darwin_drm.c b/src/amd/common/darwin/ac_darwin_drm.c
--- a/src/amd/common/darwin/ac_darwin_drm.c
+++ b/src/amd/common/darwin/ac_darwin_drm.c
@@ -501,8 +501,12 @@ acd_info(struct acd_device *dev, const struct drm_amdgpu_info *info)
    case AMDGPU_INFO_HW_IP_INFO:
       if (info->query_hw_ip.type == AMDGPU_HW_IP_GFX)
          *(struct drm_amdgpu_info_hw_ip *)out = d->hw_ip_gfx;
-      else if (info->query_hw_ip.type == AMDGPU_HW_IP_COMPUTE)
+      else if (info->query_hw_ip.type == AMDGPU_HW_IP_COMPUTE) {
          *(struct drm_amdgpu_info_hw_ip *)out = d->hw_ip_compute;
+         /* RDNA4N Submit accepts only GFX ring 0, which also handles compute dispatch. */
+         if (dev->core->kext)
+            ((struct drm_amdgpu_info_hw_ip *)out)->available_rings = 0;
+      }
       return 0;
    case AMDGPU_INFO_HW_IP_COUNT:
       *(uint32_t *)out = 1;
diff --git a/src/amd/common/darwin/libdrm_util_double_list.h b/src/amd/common/darwin/libdrm_util_double_list.h
--- a/src/amd/common/darwin/libdrm_util_double_list.h
+++ b/src/amd/common/darwin/libdrm_util_double_list.h
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@
 #ifndef libdrm_container_of /* Mesa util/macros.h has a different container_of */
 #define libdrm_container_of(ptr, sample, member)				\
     (void *)((char *)(ptr)						\
-	     - ((char *)&((__typeof__(sample))0)->member))
+	     - offsetof(__typeof__(*(sample)), member))
 #endif
 
 #define LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(pos, head, member)				\
